# What NOT to upload to EAS Build.
#
# IMPORTANT: when this file exists, EAS uses it INSTEAD OF `.gitignore` — not in
# addition to it. So everything `.gitignore` keeps out of a build has to be
# repeated here, or it starts getting uploaded.

# --- dependencies and generated output ---------------------------------------
node_modules/
.expo/
dist/
web-build/
expo-env.d.ts
*.tsbuildinfo
.expo-export-test/

# Regenerated by prebuild on the build server. Uploading a locally generated
# copy is how a stale native project silently overrides the config.
/ios
/android
.kotlin/

# --- secrets and signing ------------------------------------------------------
# The four EXPO_PUBLIC_* values come from EAS environment variables, not from a
# file in the tarball. See docs/building.md
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.jks
*.p8
*.p12
*.key
*.mobileprovision
*.pem

# --- agent tooling ------------------------------------------------------------
# Committed to the repo, but not application code — none of it is reachable from
# the bundle. It is excluded for a second, harder reason too: these directories
# contain symlinks, and EAS clones the project into a temp directory before
# uploading. Creating a symlink on Windows needs Developer Mode or elevation, so
# the clone dies with:
#
#   EPERM: operation not permitted, symlink '...\.agents\skills\banner-design'
#
# Excluding them fixes the upload and cuts the tarball substantially.
.agents/
.claude/
agent/
skills-lock.json

# --- docs ---------------------------------------------------------------------
docs/
*.orig.*
